  "body": "Was stacked on #401 (#317), now merged - this PR targets `main`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **A per-setup stock source** (`SetupDef::stock_source: Option<StockSource>`, `camcraft_app::setup_stock`): `Own` (\"Its own stock (the Stock node)\") or `FromPrevious` (\"What <previous setup> leaves behind\"). The first setup has no choice.\n- **`SetSetupStockSource`** (undoable): validated at construction - not the first setup, a carry the sim can verify (refused by name otherwise), and a real change. Undo restores the stored value, including \"never picked\". The pick rides the setup's operation stamps, so its operations go Stale.\n- **Sim** (`stock_sim_carry::entry`): `FromPrevious` carries the body (#317). `Own` keeps the M3.2 A clip when the part is held the same way, and takes a **new block** when it is held differently. When the program moves to a new block, the gouges of the block it leaves are folded into the program verdict (`fold_left`), so a gouge cut before the new block still blocks the post.\n- **Setup page** (`setup_stock_pick.rs`): the option is enabled from the second setup on. A refused carry disables it, with the reason as hover text. If the unpicked default is a refused carry, the page names the reason in error ink and points to \"Its own stock\". When the setup takes what the previous one leaves, the page shows the incoming body's box and volume and says the setup's own Stock node is not cut from (#401's reviewer note). These are measured once per document version, not every frame.\n- **Setup sheet**: STOCK prints `source   <words>` for setups after the first. For a carried stock it also prints the incoming box and volume.\n- **Project v57**: `\"stock_source\": \"own\" | \"from_previous\"`. The key is absent when the source was never picked. An unknown word is a corrupt file, refused by name. This is not breaking: v56 files load and simulate unchanged.\n\n## Default mapping (existing files are byte-identical)\n\nAn unpicked source (`None`) is #401's implicit rule:\n\n| Setup 2+ against the setup before it | Reads as | Sim |\n|---|---|---|\n| placed relative to it (#316 link, \"Same as\" included) | What it leaves behind | carry |\n| holds the part differently | What it leaves behind | carry |\n| holds the part alike, not linked | Its own stock | M3.2 A clip |\n\nNothing is written to a file or a stamp until a pick is made. The goldens are unchanged, and every `setup_carry` test passes as it did. Decisions: `docs/decisions/320-stock-source.md`.\n\n## Not in this PR\n\nThe viewport preview of the incoming body is follow-up #406. The viewport has no overlay path for a column body yet.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/setup_stock_source.rs` (new, 6): `unpicked_setups_read_the_317_rule_and_simulate_unchanged`, `a_new_block_after_a_flip_starts_from_its_own_stock_and_undoes`, `a_gouge_before_a_new_block_still_reads_in_the_verdict`, `a_refused_carry_and_the_first_setup_cannot_be_picked`, `the_pick_round_trips_and_older_or_broken_files_read_by_name`, `the_setup_sheet_states_the_stock_source`\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/setup_stock_tests.rs` (new, 3): `the_first_setup_offers_no_choice`, `picking_what_setup1_leaves_shows_the_incoming_stock_and_undoes`, `a_refused_carry_disables_the_option_with_its_reason`\n- `setup_relative`: the version assert moves from 56 to 57.\n\n## Gate (on the branch merged with current main)\n\n- app: lib (95), setup_stock_source (6), setup_carry (5), setups (11), setup_relative (8), setup_align (9), project_roundtrip (69), commands_undo (32), setup_sheet (7), stock_sim_document (9), golden_cl (23, goldens unchanged), posting (17), post_not_judged (4): all green\n- ui lib from CWD crates/ui: 308 passed, 2 ignored. No snapshot changed.\n- clippy `-D warnings` on camcraft-app and camcraft-ui, all targets: clean\n\nChangelog: A setup after the first can take its own stock or what the setup before it leaves behind; the setup page shows the incoming stock's box and volume and names why a carry is refused, and the setup sheet states the source (project v57).\n\nFixes #320\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
